title: Party Conference
subtitle: It is time for us to choose our new leader...
view-if: year = 1928 and month = 12 and z_party_leader = "Marx"
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true

= Center Party Conference

# reference: Evans, Ellen L. “Adam Stegerwald and the Role of the Christian Trade Unions in the Weimar Republic.” The Catholic Historical Review 59, no. 4 (1974): 602–26.

Wilhelm Marx, former chancellor and presidential candidate, has chosen to resign from leadership of our party. Now, we must hold a conference to replace him. This choice will determine the direction of our party going forward.

The consensus candidate on the right is Ludwig Kaas, a Catholic priest who represents our Clerical wing. He could help shore up our support among our Catholic base, and no one is terribly opposed to his candidacy. On the other hand, there is Joseph Joos, a minor leader of the Catholic trade unions, who has been more supportive of cooperation with the SPD than most. He would certainly please our Left wing, and make cooperation with the Social Democrats much easier. However, picking him would anger our Right. Said Right wing, though they are willing to support Kaas, would really rather prefer Adam Stegerwald, the head of our Catholic trade union confederation. Then again, we could always... No. It would be absurd. A horrible idea. But what if...? 

- @kaas: We will elect Ludwig Kaas as our party chair.
- @stegerwald: We will elect Adam Stegerwald as our party chair.
- @joos: We will elect Joseph Joos as our party chair.
- @papen: Against all odds and expectations, we have elected the widely-hated monarchist media baron Franz Von Papen as our party chair. God help us.
@kaas
subtitle: Kaas is an uncontroversial pick due to his religious credentials.
on-arrival: z_party_leader = "Kaas"; spd_relation -=5; right_dissent -=5; clerical_dissent -=10; catholics_z +=3;

Ludwig Kaas has been selected as our chairman. He plans to preside over a rightward turn for us, but many are happy that we are moving away from cooperating so much with the Left.
@stegerwald
subtitle: Adam Stegerwald is a dedicated anti-socialist, but also soundly pro-labour. However, he also has some slightly more controversial ideas, being in favour of interconfessionalism.
on-arrival: z_party_leader = "Stegerwald"; catholics_z -=3; new_middle_z +=4; workers_z +=10; left_dissent +=1; spd_relations -=3; tower +=1;
@joos
subtitle: Joos supports cooperation with the Social Democrats, and is popular among our Labour demographics, as well as the left wing.
on-arrival: z_party_leader = "Joos"; catholics_z +=2; workers_z +=3; right_dissent +=5; left_dissent -=5; spd_relations +=5;

Joseph Joos' election was somewhat unexpected, but not entirely. He will be a good pick to bring us closer to the Left and to the Workers of Germany. However, some on our right grumble about alleged SPD campaigning on his behalf.
@papen
choose-if: resources >= 4
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 4 : Franz Von Papen is not willing to pour enough money into his election campaign. ?]
subtitle: -4 resource. No one likes Franz Von Papen. This is a horrible decision. German democracy as we know it may just be destroyed by Franz Von Papen's election. We are never getting in a coaliton again.
on-arrival: resources -=4; z_party_leader = "Papen"; catholics_z -=5; workers_z -=3; new_middle_z -=5; old_middle_z +=4; unemployed_z -=3; left_dissent +=50; clerical_dissent +=20; right_dissent -=20; spd_relations -=50; dnvp_relations +=15; nsdap_relations +=10; hindenburg_relations +=5; ddp_relations -=50;

Franz Von Papen has done the impossible; getting people to like him. After a colossal media and lobbying campaign, Von Papen, the out-of-touch far-right media mogul who is a fan of tax cuts on the wealthy, has secured leadership of the Zentrum. Our Left wing is outraged, and our clericals aren't terribly happy either. Von Papen's first action was to cut all ties with the SPD, and begin outreach to the Far Right DNVP and NSDAP. However, Hindenburg is pleased, at least. And thank God for that, because our former coalition partners will never join us after this. 
